{"type":"message","id":"2a6e1fe6","parentId":"b82e2c67","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:28:58.671Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering diagnosis structure**\n\nI need to provide an updated diagnosis structure without recommended questions. This feels urgent! I wonder if there's a tool suitable for addressing concerns related to the kidney pipeline. Okay, I think it would be helpful to mention that there’s an option to upload the CT scan as well. This could assist in forming a clearer diagnosis. Let's move forward with this approach!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_09092fca6988da830169dcfd9ddebc8191ac5965ab5dd844c6\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp3P2gPD54SzE1kulVH2q8bTMENIZfF-NgYIqr8zVMan-sZ2ix7Ppnki-3Go9IDQd8Y1Cjd40FLPc9abHDsSZdL5Hnaagwfz3JI2vV_TSmz2-6aDRzehl0DymKn-0oQWm4Sml5FeTYj350UH9T4Ym0Ok-ohy4113rBxYmhsWi8SQmv4wvuShKYulvgywfblIX1bdvhdB8jysKUoavlMQoZbB67ZiBz0I8PBU2D2zKNkcE2W3PrmpSeGrCrDxJI8OV2L-sE6kAVdqgsfaVmnUQxdy8gx0weBcXshy2B8h3c-6BQTZ4Ls7HGCgwcF6mLAjFqKvikpusm0Q31nYHzJHhsHlRVLhwOYSPa32EEz8upXaaha2fld3IgxIsvmTquBNWU2jZS4R9oAD3maMJP8yzihTJCC31juphsxmPB3xYdieBgzw-1H_09I7sbl432-gdhQVdvU5Y0oufHAbTu6ztbPBxadm2PVdtB8489_8wlNcIX45iOR7gX8Nk7ReNVz0wuhg3xaVl6Xml7obhYf_alb_aK0Dz7hR-K6hwtlP0l1hQwudPaBJ78PD-VMK3PnIYiexX6cs-TVCeNFNcVZpFVSYr0jIYxE9BoKp41b_3Q3M8bCVhMcR-WHcEYpjnhSFIQktxUA5H-uoSMoyukqe2_PqNqBODnFQYdZVRm5uPfCTga6-kiMw7X0cy2GbqpwgZDJRH_D83mdbJXLWILdC5WBxiQDY7U4w59chnL5vbpzcuQtYnxpb-bHItwEjzP3P_-qazv32GFjoKT5awz_u6bz6vQSU1oR6D7PVQLq7eqo6zjsEHXyv8gYnxM-zdvrQLbPrqhwZOV_-vdpmBDcMEpICBgHohrxIakP1Ljqz6R4ci3jwokUOFRQ8fS8naVq2RsZDxHUcGjaW3S21ag_PukQx3CDnHQCfuXM6x0L3PHneTH60PDtUwaRZL-6cJlRM_04DBgh2m2W7RpHhMxFAd-hi2T5HCQ5sw_vMOiCF79Mxeh9Pz7Vb6OgMdgaQ1g61nVOuaFMtuZAuz-ddTiXFvXPDmKW6rVD2kMYsc50AznT55hxt2FfuSXDyA5Z0ffyodw1lqh\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering diagnosis structure**\\n\\nI need to provide an updated diagnosis structure without recommended questions. This feels urgent! I wonder if there's a tool suitable for addressing concerns related to the kidney pipeline. Okay, I think it would be helpful to mention that there’s an option to upload the CT scan as well. This could assist in forming a clearer diagnosis. Let's move forward with this approach!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Clinical picture**\nYou now report a progressively worsening, constant right-sided lower back/flank-type ache over months, visible red/pink urine, nausea/vomiting, and pain while urinating. In your structured record, there is already recent fatigue, prior mild hematuria, reduced kidney function reserve (creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 61), RCC follow-up after nephrectomy, and ongoing sunitinib treatment. Taken together, this is more concerning for a kidney/urinary tract problem than for simple muscular back pain.\n\n**Most likely possibilities**\n1. **Kidney or urinary tract obstruction/irritation**\nBlood in the urine, painful urination, nausea/vomiting, and one-sided flank/back pain can fit with a stone, clot, obstruction, or another urinary tract process affecting the right side.\n2. **Kidney infection or complicated urinary tract process**\nThis becomes more concerning if fever/chills are present, but even without those, pain with urination plus hematuria and vomiting can still reflect a significant urinary problem needing prompt assessment.\n3. **Renal cancer-related complication or recurrence-related issue**\nBecause your record includes RCC follow-up, prior nephrectomy context, and ongoing systemic treatment, recurrence or another cancer-related urinary/kidney complication cannot be excluded from symptoms alone.\n4. **Medication-related contribution**\nSunitinib can contribute to fatigue and sometimes complicate the overall picture, but it does not safely explain away the combination of hematuria, urinary pain, and unilateral pain.\n\n**Confidence / uncertainty note**\nThere is enough support here to say this needs **prompt in-person medical evaluation**, not watchful waiting. What remains uncertain is whether this is mainly obstruction, infection, treatment-related complication, or recurrence-related disease activity. You would likely need urinalysis, kidney function labs, and imaging to sort that out.\n\n**Red flags / urgent concerns**\nVisible blood in the urine + one-sided worsening pain + nausea/vomiting + pain while urinating is a red-flag combination in your situation. Because you also have reduced kidney reserve and prior RCC follow-up, I would strongly recommend **urgent same-day assessment**. If the pain becomes severe, you develop fever/chills, cannot keep fluids down, pass very little urine, feel faint, or worsen quickly, go to the **ER/emergency department now**.\n\nAt this point, the safest next step is urgent clinician review today rather than trying to manage this as routine back pain.\n\nIf you already have a **recent kidney CT scan image**, you could also use the specialized **kidney pipeline** here by uploading that CT image, and I can help summarize the preliminary imaging output. That would **not replace urgent medical evaluation**.\n\nIf you do run a diagnostic tool, I can then help you use the **LLM Distillation tool** to turn the full conversation and tool output into a clear medical summary with suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_09092fca6988da830169dcfda057dc8191aa6bac6f14975d4e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":306,"output":649,"cacheRead":16000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16955,"cost":{"input":0.0007650000000000001,"output":0.009735,"cacheRead":0.004,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0145}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776090524293}}
{"type":"message","id":"5f370647","parentId":"2a6e1fe6","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:29:26.879Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_4---8cbf8364-614a-4af4-924e-be6225c3b0b5.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_4---8cbf8364-614a-4af4-924e-be6225c3b0b5.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths — they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"387\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"sender\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Mon 2026-04-13 14:29 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Andrea Pitrone (567556397)\",\n  \"id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"name\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"username\": \"pitro_eng_guitarist\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is my CT Scan"},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1776090566877}}
{"type":"message","id":"639436d4","parentId":"5f370647","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:29:50.226Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_09092fca6988da830169dcfdd9b1ec8191a9c22cfddc2cea6a\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp3P3dVEeQxMS4r9B7oXweUsTf-bgHuySYk9qevzineYtyNc6hUwlJwEH2V80zhCMbJe_M_JWVOQtzg0Z8cb2eH6p8SXA2Nxi4HbPvPYGP2RJpyY7_o4FvQnNT_Vw-5emDYfTbBYZWKdV6lf4Ppz_oUdyVaHcmdkNwvzjFx_rMMBtTRNQoF-GRx9qQL5MLNJO6KS_5S4I0rekex3tfNUk33cICJM_r9p_vh3oGgvnSKYRbCANg5Us53VwKy_ncla7yUtDjdtLbZFhIG9_mD900Nob3bHsXWWJINxLkykGorK2MRJNYncsiQ9VhHOrv6iW0at8YkGLiramD4L4II708X6-IcEYgij9ThmtzlwZNlclQpLYKshmQr998sc-3VL-NqfKGr2HhfjCqsldi6AkqKWLyMXEKxowjq6BnfAoFtj8MOgj1hedsHkLc3XMSfg92O5nfyNIViaSiTEKziHw0UP3qCeENa81P07aHGjCcvZqFg5E8IWAC_2914LfCibNtH-zb5tEXjvBcT5os1dGAOwq068Z8Ixw94oi_tt4rgixJPfdg7EXddzaQuWEq14FVeguNBbsK804fmUuTmma6iNrVf6LBEi_mq5L4-dZTOsFCR382n5Izf3y6CE1360iRUwFyuFLBslLcO5Z7xP55eQMNgJfIn_fSQ09C5HeaiQyp0yna7ke5PNKL-DbChj556aI1t21SrTiqBr7VMtga8EPXpw772swaTVXjlz_7aSK5auw4EajdcqGJBo48nlthKPBLm5gwsi2TKSBKa37aCD3fEzRPld68NYuUmMTS-vTUFVRuTh2MjaoCSnOlinlqJ37j-_kokKQLb_jDMeTeXLd4fC4hmIeQmIoNMsv2Ptro5Zzk0w51w6y9qi4BguyWAYDuJT3WMtuEzutZDoYIsd43IQ==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I can run the kidney imaging pipeline on the CT image you just uploaded and then summarize the preliminary results clearly.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_09092fca6988da830169dcfddda27481918398a4c28aaec52e\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_23uhsoJsbGyplpQYZCndz3RD|fc_09092fca6988da830169dcfdddd3b48191b562af04d24ef0d8","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":17518,"output":83,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17601,"cost":{"input":0.043795,"output":0.001245,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.045040000000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776090566878}}
{"type":"message","id":"7e4c417a","parentId":"639436d4","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:29:50.241Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_23uhsoJsbGyplpQYZCndz3RD|fc_09092fca6988da830169dcfdddd3b48191b562af04d24ef0d8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: kidney-pipeline-execution\ndescription: Execute the kidney cancer CT pipeline by uploading a user-provided kidney CT image, taking the real uploaded image path returned by the upload endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholder inside the fixed prototype request JSON, then sending that request to the kidney pipeline execution endpoint and summarizing the Kidney Cancer Detector, Image Analyzer, and X-AI outputs. Use when a user wants to run the integrated kidney pipeline on a CT scan image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\n---\n\n# Kidney Pipeline Execution\n\nUpload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the kidney pipeline.\n\n## Required behavior\n\nFollow this sequence exactly:\n\n1. Determine the local CT image to analyze.\n   - Prefer the explicit user-provided local image path.\n   - If no path is provided, use the newest supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with `POST multipart/form-data` to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n   - Build the real remote image path as `path + filename`.\n   - Use the returned path from the upload response only.\n   - Do not keep example paths, stale upload paths, or unresolved placeholders in the executed request.\n5. Load `references/request-template.json`.\n6. Replace every <image-path-here> placeholder in the template with the real uploaded image path (rows 56, 208, 305, 371, 396).\n7. Send the resulting JSON payload to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n8. Read the pipeline response and summarize it by module:\n   - Kidney Cancer Detector\n   - Image Analyzer\n   - X-AI\n9. If the analyzer image URL exists at `response.workflows[0].branches[0].nodes[0].children[0].children[0].tracking.parameters.file_path`, extract the URL and include the image in the normal reply.\n10. Do not send out-of-band Telegram messages from the script.\n\n## Fixed values\n\nKeep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Treat the request template as a fixed prototype payload, but always inject the freshly uploaded image path before execution.\n- Fail loudly if `<image_path_here>` remains anywhere in the payload after replacement.\n- If template fields such as `filename`, `pdf_path`, or `File Path` contain placeholder or stale upload-path values, replace them with the fresh uploaded image path before execution.\n- Preserve the response wrapper shape returned by the script.\n- If the endpoint returns non-JSON text, return that text as the `response` value.\n\n## Preferred script\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script should select the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n\n## Summary fields to prioritize\n\nWhen present, summarize these fields first.\n\n### Kidney Cancer Detector\n- `Inference time`\n- `classes`\n- `confidence`\n\n### Image Analyzer\n- `cam_metrics`\n- `prediction`\n- `cam_explanation`\n- `file_path` when useful for returning the analyzer image\n\nWhen `cam_metrics` is present, include all available subfields such as:\n- `coverage`\n- `center_ratio`\n- `lr_asym`\n- `tb_asym`\n\n### X-AI\n- `confidence_interpretation`\n- `recommended_next_steps`\n- `references`\n- `summary`\n- `visual_evidence`\n\nPreserve list order for `recommended_next_steps`.\nPreserve available fields in each reference item such as `title`, `author`, `year`, and `url`.\n\n## User-facing reply rules\n\n- Group the result into the three modules.\n- Use readable labels instead of raw JSON paths.\n- Do not include low-level execution metadata by default.\n- Mention clearly that the pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n- Append the analyzer image itself when an analyzer image URL is available.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1776090590236}}
