properly, so I’m considering suggesting the distillation tool next since that ran earlier. It’ll help refine the information and make it clearer. So, let's make sure everything is set up nicely for the user!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Kidney Cancer Detector**\nThe pipeline classified this CT image as **kidney tumor** with **very high model confidence (99.99%)**.\nInference time: **3.22 seconds**.\n\n**Image Analyzer**\nThe image analyzer also predicted **kidney_tumor**.\nIts heatmap focused on a **small, localized peripheral renal region** with an asymmetric pattern, which the model interpreted as a possible focal structural abnormality.\nCAM coverage: **0.0322**\nCAM center ratio: **0.0495**\nCAM left-right asymmetry: **0.5446**\nCAM top-bottom asymmetry: **1.0000**\nA heatmap image is attached below for reference.\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/18def15f-36ce-4ad3-9f26-1955506785be.jpg\n\n**xAI**\nThe explanation module says the result is **high-confidence** but still needs confirmation with standard medical evaluation.\nSummary: the uploaded image is considered **likely related to kidney cancer** by the pipeline.\nVisual evidence: the model identified an area that may correspond to a **kidney tumor**.\n\n**Result Interpretation**\nThis tool output is **concerning** and it is also broadly consistent with the symptom pattern you reported earlier: worsening right-sided flank/back pain, visible blood in the urine, nausea/vomiting, and pain while urinating.\nBecause of your prior RCC follow-up history, this combination should be treated as something that needs **urgent in-person medical assessment**.\nThat said, this pipeline is only a **preliminary signal**, not an actual diagnosis. A clinician would still need to confirm with proper radiology review, examination, urinalysis, blood tests, and likely formal CT/MRI interpretation.\n\n**Recommended next steps**\n1. **Seek urgent medical evaluation today**, and if symptoms worsen, go to the **ER/emergency department**.\n2. Bring or send the CT scan to your **urologist/oncologist** for formal review as soon as possible.\n3. Ask for **urinalysis, kidney function labs, and imaging review** promptly.\n4. If you develop **fever, severe pain, reduced urine output, faintness, or inability to keep fluids down**, go to emergency care immediately.\n\nPlease remember: this tool output is a **preliminary signal, not a diagnosis**.\n\nSince you have now run a diagnostic tool, I also suggest using the **LLM Distillation tool** next so I can help turn the symptom discussion plus this imaging result into one clear medical report with suggested next steps.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_09092fca6988da830169dcfe055d688191abe9a1d127999e2e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9440,"output":614,"cacheRead":18560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28614,"cost":{"input":0.023600000000000003,"output":0.00921,"cacheRead":0.00464,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.037450000000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776090624938}}
